// Business & technology terms
:keywords: CloneZilla, disk imaging, disk cloning, savedisk, restoredisk, device-image, local_dev, recovery, backup, disaster recovery, free software, open source, GNU/Linux
// The purpose of this script
:summary: A step-by-step filming script that shows how I create a full disk image with CloneZilla Live, and then how I use that image to restore a system - with explicit, repeated disclaimers about the destructive nature of restoring a disk.
// An outline of this script
:description: Cold open hooks the viewer on total disk failure. Scene 1 frames the conflict: one bad day, everything gone unless I have a backup. Scene 2 covers preparing and booting the CloneZilla live rescue disk. Scene 3 walks through saving a whole disk as an image on a second disk (device-image -> local_dev -> sdb1 -> savedisk). Scene 4 delivers the disclaimers: restoring overwrites everything on the target disk. Scene 5 walks through restoring the image onto a fresh disk (restoredisk). Scene 6 recaps, delivers the core promise, the Call To Action, and the Signature Sign Off.
// Attributions are `None` or URLs to the source material
:attributions: https://clonezilla.org/clonezilla-live-doc.php
// Status is `Pending`, `In progress`, or `Complete`
:status: In progress
