// ======================================================================
// VIDEO PRODUCTION METADATA
// These attributes are consumed by the AI agent that processes the
// (pending) placeholders. They carry the aesthetic, scope, and
// guidance that is deliberately NOT repeated in the body of the script.
// ======================================================================
// The default product type this template is geared toward
:videoType: YouTube explainer video
// The core topic, as supplied by the producer
:coreTopic: Creating and restoring a disk image with CloneZilla Live
// The source material, as supplied by the producer
:sourceMaterial: The CloneZilla Live documentation (https://clonezilla.org/clonezilla-live-doc.php), specifically the "Save disk image" and "Restore disk image" step-by-step docs
// The single most important sentence of the video: the core promise.
// It should be crystal clear, compelling, outcome-focused, and bolded
// wherever it is delivered.
:corePromise: I can save my whole disk as one image with CloneZilla, and when disaster strikes, I restore that image onto a fresh disk and my system is back
// The default framework. Storytelling is best suited to explainer videos.
:framework: Storytelling
// The storytelling arc mapped onto an explainer video
:frameworkArc: Hook (cold open) -> Conflict (the setup and the problem) -> Resolution (the value delivery across the scenes) -> Lesson (the payoff in the review)
// Baseline video runtime. Longer runtimes are expected for more complex topics.
:targetRuntime: 12 minutes (baseline extended for a two-part walkthrough: image plus restore)
// Word count is not a constraint. It guides the creation process, it does not limit it.
:wordCountPolicy: A script is as long as it needs to be; no word-count ceiling applies
// Speaking pace, 130-160 words per minute, is a reference for estimating
// screen time in the Duration columns, not a cap on any placeholder.
:pacing: 130-160 words per minute (a reference value for the Duration estimates, not a limitation)
// The number of scenes is structure, not a boundary
:sceneGuidance: One Scene section per beat of the {frameworkArc}; repeat the Scene section as many times as the topic needs
// Voice-over style, applied to every placeholder in the body.
// Explainer videos can be dry, technical, and boring - this template
// refuses any of that.
:voiceOverStyle: Energetic, punchy, enthusiastic, minimal filler
// Writing guidance for the AI agent (from the style guide article and house style)
:writingGuidance: Write the way you speak; short sentences, natural rhythm; every sentence earns its place; use open loops, curiosity gaps, and pattern interrupts; keep transitions quick; read the script aloud and time it; avoid rambling, repetition, over-explaining, and long intros
// Order of the script, immutable
:structure: Cold open -> Title sequence -> Scenes -> Review
// ======================================================================
// SCOPE OF THE COLD OPEN AND REVIEW
// ======================================================================
// The cold open is a teaser of the up-coming content. Its purpose is to
// engage the viewer, nail their attention, and hook them - all with the
// hook delivered in approximately 15 seconds - and to deliver the
// Signature Sign On, all before the title sequence rolls.
:coldOpenScope: A teaser of the up-coming content that hooks the viewer within 15 seconds, nails their attention, seeds the core promise {corePromise}, and ends with the immutable Signature Sign On {signOn}; it is the pre-cursor to the title sequence
// Hook techniques, from the style guide
:coldOpenTechniques: A specific promise, a curiosity gap, immediate value, or a bold claim
// The review is a quick recap of the video that pays off the core
// promise, followed by the Call To Action and the Signature Sign Off.
:reviewScope: A quick, punchy recap of the video that pays off the core promise {corePromise}, followed by the immutable CTA {cta} and the immutable Signature Sign Off {signOff}
// ======================================================================
// IMMUTABLES - deliver verbatim, word for word, never paraphrased
// ======================================================================
:signOn: My name is Brian, I'm an AI Generalist, and this is DigitalCoreNZ
:cta: Click the Like button, and Subscribe for more content, if this is the kind of video you enjoy.
:signOff: Until next time: Be safe, be kind, be awesome, kia kaha!!

